# Services & API

## Domain folder shape

Each domain under [`app/services/<domain>/`](mdc:app/services/):

```
api/*.api.ts      # HTTP via apiFetch (auth uses authFetch)
types/*.types.ts  # + types/index.ts
helpers/*.helper.js
index.ts          # re-export api + types + helpers
```

Reports nest further: `services/reports/{admin|branch|customer-service|shared}/`.  
Example barrel: [`app/services/user/index.ts`](mdc:app/services/user/index.ts).

## Calling the API

- Use [`apiFetch`](mdc:app/utils/apiFetch.ts) / helpers `asList`, `asData`, `asPaginated`, `firstRow`
- Do **not** raw-`$fetch` the Nest API from components — go through `*Api` modules
- Auth: Bearer token from localStorage (handled in `apiFetch`); public allowlist includes `/auth/login`
- `academicYearId` query is attached automatically when stored
- [`useApi.js`](mdc:app/composables/useApi.js) exists but is unused — prefer `*Api` + `apiFetch`, do not revive it for new work

```ts
// ✅
export const userApi = {
  async getUsers(params: UserQuery = {}): Promise<UserResponse[]> {
    return asList<UserResponse>(
      await apiFetch("/users", { method: "GET", params }),
    );
  },
};

// ❌ fetch/axios directly, or duplicate Authorization headers in every call
```

## Helpers vs UI

- Form mapping / list normalize / query builders → `helpers/*.helper.js`
- Keep Vue components thin: call service exports, don’t embed endpoint paths
